# dev server — `npm run dev` → bin/streamo.js --env-file env/dev.env
#
# ⚠️ IT STARTS, IT SERVES, AND ON THE SECOND START IT DELETES YOUR FILES.
#    Measured 2026-08-04: 154 files under public/ → 39. Silently, no error.
#    Everything is tracked, so `git checkout -- public/` restores it — and see
#    RECOVERY below, because restoring with the server *down* doesn't stick.
#
# WHAT ACTUALLY HAPPENS, in order:
#
#   1. Against a FRESH archive it works. Real bytes for /, /streamo/h.js,
#      /apps/explorer/index.html, /apps/grove/index.html. This is the run that
#      looks like success, and it is the run that arms the trap: it writes
#      shard Records, some of them empty.
#   2. On the NEXT start, fileSync reconciles those empty shards against a
#      populated disk — and the empty Record wins. Your files go.
#
# THE DEFECT, precisely: fileSync cannot tell "this Record is empty" from
# "this Record was never populated." On the read path that same ambiguity is
# only misleading (`_materialize` serves `200 null` for a Record it has never
# heard of). On the write path it destroys.
#
# WHY IT CURRENTLY CRASHES INSTEAD, and why that is on purpose: a keyless
# `ours: true` mount is never marked writable, so writeMany aborts with
# "mounted Record for 'apps/explorer/' is not Writable". That stop is ugly and
# it is LOAD-BEARING — it fires before anything can be deleted. `bc6e5e0`
# removed it and was reverted in `3b6975d` for exactly that reason. Fix the
# empty-vs-unpopulated ambiguity FIRST, then re-land bc6e5e0.
#
# RECOVERY, if it already happened: restore **while the server is running** —
# David, 2026-08-04. fileSync follows whichever side changed, so files
# reappearing on disk get written INTO the Record, which repairs it. Restoring
# with the server stopped leaves the empty Record intact to do it again.
# Nuclear option: move .streamo/<homekey>.bin aside; it rebuilds from disk.
# One is already quarantined at .streamo-quarantine/ from 08-04.
#
# The mount keys were dropped in 951c5e1 — they were prod-derived and every
# one mismatched under dev. That also removed a tripwire: nothing now catches
# a wrong identity silently authoring a parallel tree.
#
STREAMO_NAME=streamo-dev
STREAMO_USERNAME=dev
STREAMO_PASSWORD=dev
STREAMO_KEY_ITERATIONS=1
STREAMO_FEED=streamo.dev
STREAMO_FILES=public
STREAMO_WEB=8080

# Attach a REPL to the running dev server:
#
#     npm run dev:repl          (or: nc -U /tmp/streamo-dev.sock)
#
# Multiple connections are fine and disconnecting doesn't kill the server, so
# you can attach, poke, Ctrl-D, and come back. `globalThis` carries `record`,
# `registry`, `folder` (path-shaped: `await folder.resolvePath('public/…')`,
# `folder.mounts()`, `folder.files()`), `signer`, and the `get/set/merge/ls`
# shorthands — the banner it prints on connect lists all of them.
#
# This is the cheapest way to answer "what is actually in the Record" without
# curling and squinting at JSON, which is how an evening got spent on 08-03.
STREAMO_REPL_SOCKET=/tmp/streamo-dev.sock
